     "value": "All structural data were processed with voxel-based morphometry toolbox VBM5.1 and the Statistical Parametric Mapping SPM5 software package. The VBM toolbox combines tissue segmentation, bias correction and spatial normalization into a unified model. A Hidden Markov Random Field model was used to introduce spatial constraints into the segmentation process. Images were multiplied (modulated) by the Jacobian determinants from the normalization step to preserve volume information, and modulated gray matter images were smoothed with a 12 mm full width at half maximum Gaussian kernel.",
